# Agentic Framework for Claude — MCP environment variables
#
# These are OS-level environment variables, read directly by MCP servers at
# launch time (not an installer-time .env file — nothing here is copied,
# parsed, or expanded during install). Set them in your shell profile, your
# OS environment, or via /agentic-framework:setup, before starting a
# Claude Code session that loads the agentic-framework plugin.

# Context7 API key (optional). The context7 MCP server works keyless with
# lower rate limits; set this for higher limits.
# Get your key from: https://context7.com/dashboard
# CONTEXT7_API_KEY=

# Root directory the filesystem MCP server is allowed to access (optional).
# Defaults to the current project directory (CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR) when unset.
# MCP_FS_ROOT=

# --- Model-tier guard (read by the pretooluse-model-guard hook, not by an MCP server) ---
# The hook denies a sub-agent call that would run on the orchestrator's top
# model tier: a `model` naming that tier, any `fork`, and a built-in agent
# (Explore, Plan, general-purpose) spawned with no `model`.

# User-side floor (a Claude Code variable; set it in your settings `env` or
# your OS environment). Any agent without a tier of its own then resolves to
# this model instead of inheriting the parent's, and the guard stops asking for
# an explicit model on built-in agents.
# CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL=sonnet

# Escape hatch: `off` disables the guard entirely (case-insensitive). Like the
# variable above, set it in your Claude Code settings `env` or your OS
# environment; nothing reads a `.env` file into a hook's environment.
# AF_MODEL_GUARD=off
